{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785692048649,"sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_pBL3cbpQA01uRSwaHSNBp7qn","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/fanout/fanout-run-cli-lineage-spawn.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/fanout/fanout-run-cli-lineage-spawn.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"DLR-025 -- Fan-out CLI lineage driver spawn and isolation\"\n3: description: \"Validate fanout-run.cjs creates per-lineage dirs with isolated .executor-state paths, saves stdout to logs/, writes orchestration summary and ledger, and returns early for native-only configs.\"\n4: version: 1.4.0.4\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # DLR-025 -- Fan-out CLI lineage driver spawn and isolation\n8: \n9: This document captures the validation contract, execution flow, and metadata for `DLR-025`.\n10: \n11: ---\n12: \n13: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n14: \n15: Validates the CLI lineage pool driver `fanout-run.cjs` — specifically lineage dir creation,\n16: per-kind state-dir isolation, stdout capture, and orchestration artifacts.\n17: \n18: ### Why This Matters\n19: \n20: This is the script that dispatches all CLI executor fan-out lineages. If the per-kind\n21: `SPECKIT_<KIND>_STATE_DIR` is not set per-lineage, same-kind replicas collide on lockfiles.\n22: If stdout is not saved, the salvage sweep has nothing to recover from.\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n27: \n28: - Objective: Confirm `fanout-run.cjs` creates distinct per-lineage dirs and state dirs, writes orchestration artifacts, and returns early for native-only configs.\n29: - Layer partition: CLI lineage dispatch.\n30: - Real user request: `Validate the fan-out CLI lineage driver and confirm the 5 integration tests pass, verifying lineage isolation and orchestration artifact creation.`\n31: - Expected signals: `lineages/lineage-a/` and `lineages/lineage-b/` dirs created; `.executor-state/` paths distinct for same-kind replicas; `orchestration-summary.json` present with `total_cli_lineages=2`; `orchestration-status.log` has JSONL events; native-only config returns `{status:\"ok\", results:[]}`.\n32: - Pass/fail: PASS only if all 5 tests pass with EXIT 0 and source inspection confirms `SPECKIT_STATE_ENV_BY_KIND` usage; FAIL otherwise.\n33: \n34: ---\n35: \n36: ## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n37: \n38: ### Prerequisites\n39: \n40: - Working directory is repository root.\n41: - `scripts/fanout-run.cjs` and `scripts/fanout-salvage.cjs` present.\n42: \n43: ### Steps\n44: \n45: 1. Inspect `scripts/fanout-run.cjs` — confirm `SPECKIT_STATE_ENV_BY_KIND` map, `computeLineageTimeoutMs` formula, `buildLineageCommand` per-kind branch.\n46: 2. Verify `extraEnv` in the worker sets both `SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID` and the kind-specific state dir var.\n47: 3. `bash: cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server && npx vitest run ../../runtime//tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts`\n48: 4. Confirm 5 tests pass. Note: the 2-lineage stub test verifies dirs, ledger, and summary; the lockfile-isolation test verifies `.executor-state` paths are distinct for same-kind replicas.\n49: \n50: ### Expected Outcome\n51: \n52: 5/5 pass. Lineage dirs created, `.executor-state` dirs distinct, `orchestration-summary.json` with `total_cli_lineages=2`, JSONL ledger written, native-only config returns early without spawning.\n53: \n54: ### Failure Modes\n55: \n56: - Missing `SPECKIT_<KIND>_STATE_DIR` in env: same-kind replicas use the same state dir and may trip the loop-lock.\n57: - stdout not saved to `logs/fanout-lineage.out`: salvage sweep has no data to recover from.\n58: - Pool worker throws instead of settling: pool fails entirely rather than reporting per-item status.\n59: \n60: ---\n61: \n62: ## 4. SOURCE ANCHORS\n63: \n64: ### Implementation\n65: \n66: | File | Role |\n67: |---|---|\n68: | `scripts/fanout-run.cjs` | CLI arg parsing, pool orchestration, per-kind command construction, stdout capture, salvage call |\n69: | `scripts/fanout-salvage.cjs` | Salvage called in worker after subprocess exits |\n70: | `scripts/fanout-pool.cjs` | `runCappedPool` + ledger used by the driver |\n71: \n72: ### Validation\n73: \n74: | File | Role |\n75: |---|---|\n76: | `tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts` | 5 integration tests with stub CLI binaries |\n77: \n78: ---\n79: \n80: ## 5. SOURCE_METADATA\n81: \n82: - Group: Fan-Out\n83: - Playbook ID: DLR-025\n84: - Feature catalog entry: `feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md`\n85: - Scenario file path: `manual-testing-playbook/fanout/fanout-run-cli-lineage-spawn.md`\n86: - Expected verdict mode: GREEN when 5/5 pass and source anchors agree\n87: - Wall-time estimate: 5-10 min\n\n(End of file - total 87 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"DLR-025 -- Fan-out CLI lineage driver spawn and isolation\"\ndescription: \"Validate fanout-run.cjs creates per-lineage dirs with isolated .executor-state paths, saves stdout to logs/, writes orchestration summary and ledger, and returns early for native-only configs.\"\nversion: 1.4.0.4\n---\n\n# DLR-025 -- Fan-out CLI lineage driver spawn and isolation\n\nThis document captures the validation contract, execution flow, and metadata for `DLR-025`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nValidates the CLI lineage pool driver `fanout-run.cjs` — specifically lineage dir creation,\nper-kind state-dir isolation, stdout capture, and orchestration artifacts.\n\n### Why This Matters\n\nThis is the script that dispatches all CLI executor fan-out lineages. If the per-kind","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/fanout/fanout-run-cli-lineage-spawn.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"DLR-025 -- Fan-out CLI lineage driver spawn and isolation\"\ndescription: \"Validate fanout-run.cjs creates per-lineage dirs with isolated .executor-state paths, saves stdout to logs/, writes orchestration summary and ledger, and returns early for native-only configs.\"\nversion: 1.4.0.4\n---\n\n# DLR-025 -- Fan-out CLI lineage driver spawn and isolation\n\nThis document captures the validation contract, execution flow, and metadata for `DLR-025`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nValidates the CLI lineage pool driver `fanout-run.cjs` — specifically lineage dir creation,\nper-kind state-dir isolation, stdout capture, and orchestration artifacts.\n\n### Why This Matters\n\nThis is the script that dispatches all CLI executor fan-out lineages. If the per-kind\n`SPECKIT_<KIND>_STATE_DIR` is not set per-lineage, same-kind replicas collide on lockfiles.\nIf stdout is not saved, the salvage sweep has nothing to recover from.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SCENARIO CONTRACT\n\n- Objective: Confirm `fanout-run.cjs` creates distinct per-lineage dirs and state dirs, writes orchestration artifacts, and returns early for native-only configs.\n- Layer partition: CLI lineage dispatch.\n- Real user request: `Validate the fan-out CLI lineage driver and confirm the 5 integration tests pass, verifying lineage isolation and orchestration artifact creation.`\n- Expected signals: `lineages/lineage-a/` and `lineages/lineage-b/` dirs created; `.executor-state/` paths distinct for same-kind replicas; `orchestration-summary.json` present with `total_cli_lineages=2`; `orchestration-status.log` has JSONL events; native-only config returns `{status:\"ok\", results:[]}`.\n- Pass/fail: PASS only if all 5 tests pass with EXIT 0 and source inspection confirms `SPECKIT_STATE_ENV_BY_KIND` usage; FAIL otherwise.\n\n---\n\n## 3. TEST EXECUTION\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- Working directory is repository root.\n- `scripts/fanout-run.cjs` and `scripts/fanout-salvage.cjs` present.\n\n### Steps\n\n1. Inspect `scripts/fanout-run.cjs` — confirm `SPECKIT_STATE_ENV_BY_KIND` map, `computeLineageTimeoutMs` formula, `buildLineageCommand` per-kind branch.\n2. Verify `extraEnv` in the worker sets both `SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID` and the kind-specific state dir var.\n3. `bash: cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server && npx vitest run ../../runtime//tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts`\n4. Confirm 5 tests pass. Note: the 2-lineage stub test verifies dirs, ledger, and summary; the lockfile-isolation test verifies `.executor-state` paths are distinct for same-kind replicas.\n\n### Expected Outcome\n\n5/5 pass. Lineage dirs created, `.executor-state` dirs distinct, `orchestration-summary.json` with `total_cli_lineages=2`, JSONL ledger written, native-only config returns early without spawning.\n\n### Failure Modes\n\n- Missing `SPECKIT_<KIND>_STATE_DIR` in env: same-kind replicas use the same state dir and may trip the loop-lock.\n- stdout not saved to `logs/fanout-lineage.out`: salvage sweep has no data to recover from.\n- Pool worker throws instead of settling: pool fails entirely rather than reporting per-item status.\n\n---\n\n## 4. SOURCE ANCHORS\n\n### Implementation\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `scripts/fanout-run.cjs` | CLI arg parsing, pool orchestration, per-kind command construction, stdout capture, salvage call |\n| `scripts/fanout-salvage.cjs` | Salvage called in worker after subprocess exits |\n| `scripts/fanout-pool.cjs` | `runCappedPool` + ledger used by the driver |\n\n### Validation\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/fanout-run.vitest.ts` | 5 integration tests with stub CLI binaries |\n\n---\n\n## 5. SOURCE_METADATA\n\n- Group: Fan-Out\n- Playbook ID: DLR-025\n- Feature catalog entry: `feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md`\n- Scenario file path: `manual-testing-playbook/fanout/fanout-run-cli-lineage-spawn.md`\n- Expected verdict mode: GREEN when 5/5 pass and source anchors agree\n- Wall-time estimate: 5-10 min","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":87,"totalLines":87,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/manual-testing-playbook/fanout/fanout-run-cli-lineage-spawn.md","time":{"start":1785692048637,"end":1785692048645}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07f4a5a4ca917c6f016a6f7f8fc4448191a62f7cffc415ac4f"}},"id":"prt_fc38a49d2001mTIMKOsqZZp00k","sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","messageID":"msg_fc38a3af9001tjJUoKWXzOqgJL"}}
