{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785692184177,"sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_ViWSjsaTJhmAdFwWhPUFdMJA","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/findings-registry.json"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/findings-registry.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"openQuestions\": [],\n3:   \"resolvedQuestions\": [\n4:     {\"id\": \"Q1\", \"text\": \"Which MCP 2.0 actions are read-only, draft-safe, destructive, publish-capable, or deployment-capable?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Operation classes enumerated per module/action in research.md Section 4; publishing always explicit; CMS mutations can hit live site\"},\n5:     {\"id\": \"Q2\", \"text\": \"Does the official surface use remote OAuth, a local server, an API token, or a client-specific connection flow?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Remote OAuth (mcp.webflow.com/sse, mcp-remote experimental) OR local bearer token (site/workspace/OAuth) via WEBFLOW_TOKEN; no client-specific flow\"},\n6:     {\"id\": \"Q3\", \"text\": \"Is mcp-webflow a workflow or a transport?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Transport: hub transport-leaf layout; mutations land in Webflow cloud; run_workflow executes Webflow-side managed workflows\"},\n7:     {\"id\": \"Q4\", \"text\": \"What non-production Webflow workspace or site can support live smoke?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Dedicated test workspace + test site; read-only scopes baseline; publish only to publishToWebflowSubdomain (staging), single page, 1/min\"},\n8:     {\"id\": \"Q5\", \"text\": \"Which Webflow operations require explicit operator confirmation, and which require a named rollback?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Publish/destructive/deploy classes confirmation-gated; staged-first rollback; API-level site restore UNKNOWN\"},\n9:     {\"id\": \"Q6\", \"text\": \"Which operations must pair with sk-design design judgment?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Designer-family (deElement/deStyle/deVariable/deComponents/deAsset, update_page_settings) pair with sk-design; Data-family operations do not\"}\n10:   ],\n11:   \"keyFindings\": [\n12:     {\"id\": \"F1\", \"run\": 1, \"finding\": \"Official server is webflow/mcp-server (npm webflow-mcp-server 1.0.1, MIT); MCP SDK 1.25.2 + webflow-api 3.2.1\", \"sources\": [\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/package.json\"]},\n13:     {\"id\": \"F2\", \"run\": 1, \"finding\": \"Two connection modes: remote OAuth at https://mcp.webflow.com/sse (no bridge app for most actions) and local npx webflow-mcp-server with WEBFLOW_TOKEN\", \"sources\": [\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md\"]},\n14:     {\"id\": \"F3\", \"run\": 1, \"finding\": \"18 tool modules; de* are Designer/bridge-bound\", \"sources\": [\"https://api.github.com/repos/webflow/mcp-server/git/trees/main?recursive=1\"]},\n15:     {\"id\": \"F4\", \"run\": 2, \"finding\": \"Full action inventory with operation classes (read-only/draft-safe/destructive/publish/deploy) extracted from src/tools/*.ts\", \"sources\": [\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/*.ts\"]},\n16:     {\"id\": \"F5\", \"run\": 3, \"finding\": \"Remote auth is mcp-remote (experimental); role gate owner/admin only; rate limits 60/120 rpm plan-based; site publish 1/min\", \"sources\": [\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md\", \"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rate-limits.md\"]},\n17:     {\"id\": \"F6\", \"run\": 4, \"finding\": \"Scopes table; workspace tokens lack site scope; publishToWebflowSubdomain = staging target\", \"sources\": [\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/scopes.md\", \"https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/sites/publish.md\"]},\n18:     {\"id\": \"F7\", \"run\": 5, \"finding\": \"mcp-webflow is a transport (hub leaf layout); confirmation classes; sk-design pairing boundary\", \"sources\": [\"file:.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/\"]}\n19:   ],\n20:   \"ruledOutDirections\": [\n21:     {\"approach\": \"npm webflow-mcp as server package\", \"reason\": \"Third-party package unrelated to official server\", \"run\": 1},\n22:     {\"approach\": \"Workspace token as general write credential\", \"reason\": \"No site scope; docs recommend read-only\", \"run\": 4},\n23:     {\"approach\": \"API site duplication/backup for test scaffolding\", \"reason\": \"Not part of Data API v2 surface\", \"run\": 4},\n24:     {\"approach\": \"Classify mcp-webflow as a workflow system\", \"reason\": \"Transport executes Webflow-side workflows; does not orchestrate\", \"run\": 5},\n25:     {\"approach\": \"Treat CMS mutations as implicitly draft-safe\", \"reason\": \"Official FAQ: live-site create/delete possible\", \"run\": 3}\n26:   ],\n27:   \"blockedStops\": []\n28: }\n\n(End of file - total 28 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"openQuestions\": [],\n  \"resolvedQuestions\": [\n    {\"id\": \"Q1\", \"text\": \"Which MCP 2.0 actions are read-only, draft-safe, destructive, publish-capable, or deployment-capable?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Operation classes enumerated per module/action in research.md Section 4; publishing always explicit; CMS mutations can hit live site\"},\n    {\"id\": \"Q2\", \"text\": \"Does the official surface use remote OAuth, a local server, an API token, or a client-specific connection flow?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Remote OAuth (mcp.webflow.com/sse, mcp-remote experimental) OR local bearer token (site/workspace/OAuth) via WEBFLOW_TOKEN; no client-specific flow\"},\n    {\"id\": \"Q3\", \"text\": \"Is mcp-webflow a workflow or a transport?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Transport: hub transport-leaf layout; mutations land in Webflow cloud; run_workflow executes Webflow-side managed workflows\"},\n    {\"id\": \"Q4\", \"text\": \"What non-production Webflow workspace or site can support live smoke?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Dedicated test workspace + test site; read-only scopes baseline; publish only to publishToWebflowSubdomain (staging), single page, 1/min\"},\n    {\"id\": \"Q5\", \"text\": \"Which Webflow operations require explicit operator confirmation, and which require a named rollback?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Publish/destructive/deploy classes confirmation-gated; staged-first rollback; API-level site restore UNKNOWN\"},\n    {\"id\": \"Q6\", \"text\": \"Which operations must pair with sk-design design judgment?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Designer-family (deElement/deStyle/deVariable/deComponents/deAsset, update_page_settings) pair with sk-design; Data-family operations do not\"}\n  ],\n  \"keyFindings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"F1\", \"run\": 1, \"finding\": \"Official server is webflow/mcp-server (npm webflow-mcp-server 1.0.1, MIT); MCP SDK 1.25.2 + webflow-api 3.2.1\", \"sources\": [\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/package.json\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"F2\", \"run\": 1, \"finding\": \"Two connection modes: remote OAuth at https://mcp.webflow.com/sse (no bridge app for most actions) and local npx webflow-mcp-server with WEBFLOW_TOKEN\", \"sources\": [\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"F3\", \"run\": 1, \"finding\": \"18 tool modules; de* are Designer/bridge-bound\", \"sources\": [\"https://api.github.com/repos/webflow/mcp-server/git/trees/main?recursive=1\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"F4\", \"run\": 2, \"finding\": \"Full action inventory with operation classes (read-only/draft-safe/destructive/publish/deploy) extracted from src/tools/*.ts\", \"sources\": [\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/*.ts\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"F5\", \"run\": 3, \"finding\": \"Remote auth is mcp-remote (experimental); role gate owner/admin only; rate limits 60/120 rpm plan-based; site publish 1/min\", \"sources\": [\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md\", \"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rate-limits.md\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"F6\", \"run\": 4, \"finding\": \"Scopes table; workspace tokens lack site scope; publishToWebflowSubdomain = staging target\", \"sources\": [\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/scopes.md\", \"https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/sites/publish.md\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"F7\", \"run\": 5, \"finding\": \"mcp-webflow is a transport (hub leaf layout); confirmation classes; sk-design pairing boundary\", \"sources\": [\"file:.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/\"]}\n  ],\n  \"ruledOutDirections\": [","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/findings-registry.json","text":"{\n  \"openQuestions\": [],\n  \"resolvedQuestions\": [\n    {\"id\": \"Q1\", \"text\": \"Which MCP 2.0 actions are read-only, draft-safe, destructive, publish-capable, or deployment-capable?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Operation classes enumerated per module/action in research.md Section 4; publishing always explicit; CMS mutations can hit live site\"},\n    {\"id\": \"Q2\", \"text\": \"Does the official surface use remote OAuth, a local server, an API token, or a client-specific connection flow?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Remote OAuth (mcp.webflow.com/sse, mcp-remote experimental) OR local bearer token (site/workspace/OAuth) via WEBFLOW_TOKEN; no client-specific flow\"},\n    {\"id\": \"Q3\", \"text\": \"Is mcp-webflow a workflow or a transport?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Transport: hub transport-leaf layout; mutations land in Webflow cloud; run_workflow executes Webflow-side managed workflows\"},\n    {\"id\": \"Q4\", \"text\": \"What non-production Webflow workspace or site can support live smoke?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Dedicated test workspace + test site; read-only scopes baseline; publish only to publishToWebflowSubdomain (staging), single page, 1/min\"},\n    {\"id\": \"Q5\", \"text\": \"Which Webflow operations require explicit operator confirmation, and which require a named rollback?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Publish/destructive/deploy classes confirmation-gated; staged-first rollback; API-level site restore UNKNOWN\"},\n    {\"id\": \"Q6\", \"text\": \"Which operations must pair with sk-design design judgment?\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"answer\": \"Designer-family (deElement/deStyle/deVariable/deComponents/deAsset, update_page_settings) pair with sk-design; Data-family operations do not\"}\n  ],\n  \"keyFindings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"F1\", \"run\": 1, \"finding\": \"Official server is webflow/mcp-server (npm webflow-mcp-server 1.0.1, MIT); MCP SDK 1.25.2 + webflow-api 3.2.1\", \"sources\": [\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/package.json\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"F2\", \"run\": 1, \"finding\": \"Two connection modes: remote OAuth at https://mcp.webflow.com/sse (no bridge app for most actions) and local npx webflow-mcp-server with WEBFLOW_TOKEN\", \"sources\": [\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/README.md\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"F3\", \"run\": 1, \"finding\": \"18 tool modules; de* are Designer/bridge-bound\", \"sources\": [\"https://api.github.com/repos/webflow/mcp-server/git/trees/main?recursive=1\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"F4\", \"run\": 2, \"finding\": \"Full action inventory with operation classes (read-only/draft-safe/destructive/publish/deploy) extracted from src/tools/*.ts\", \"sources\": [\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webflow/mcp-server/main/src/tools/*.ts\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"F5\", \"run\": 3, \"finding\": \"Remote auth is mcp-remote (experimental); role gate owner/admin only; rate limits 60/120 rpm plan-based; site publish 1/min\", \"sources\": [\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md\", \"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rate-limits.md\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"F6\", \"run\": 4, \"finding\": \"Scopes table; workspace tokens lack site scope; publishToWebflowSubdomain = staging target\", \"sources\": [\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/scopes.md\", \"https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/sites/publish.md\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"F7\", \"run\": 5, \"finding\": \"mcp-webflow is a transport (hub leaf layout); confirmation classes; sk-design pairing boundary\", \"sources\": [\"file:.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/\"]}\n  ],\n  \"ruledOutDirections\": [\n    {\"approach\": \"npm webflow-mcp as server package\", \"reason\": \"Third-party package unrelated to official server\", \"run\": 1},\n    {\"approach\": \"Workspace token as general write credential\", \"reason\": \"No site scope; docs recommend read-only\", \"run\": 4},\n    {\"approach\": \"API site duplication/backup for test scaffolding\", \"reason\": \"Not part of Data API v2 surface\", \"run\": 4},\n    {\"approach\": \"Classify mcp-webflow as a workflow system\", \"reason\": \"Transport executes Webflow-side workflows; does not orchestrate\", \"run\": 5},\n    {\"approach\": \"Treat CMS mutations as implicitly draft-safe\", \"reason\": \"Official FAQ: live-site create/delete possible\", \"run\": 3}\n  ],\n  \"blockedStops\": []\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":28,"totalLines":28,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/findings-registry.json","time":{"start":1785692184158,"end":1785692184172}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0e82b5215f04ee4c016a6f801804dc81919a6fd5e74d5cef24"}},"id":"prt_fc38c5e5a001ow36tZpLymUL4F","sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","messageID":"msg_fc38c311c001q7qttDE6L1zQl8"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785692184177,"sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_a6sf4fHJento7bwippGUzBUj","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/deep-research-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deep Research Strategy - deepseek-max lineage\n2: \n3: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n4: \n5: Detached fan-out lineage for the 015-mcp-webflow Phase 1 research run. Executor: cli-pi (deepseek-v4-flash). Stop policy: max-iterations (5), convergence off (telemetry only). Status: COMPLETE — synthesis written, config.status=complete.\n6: \n7: ## 2. TOPIC\n8: \n9: Webflow MCP 2.0 — synthesize capabilities, constraints, and recommendations from official and corroborating sources.\n10: \n11: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n12: \n13: (none — all six answered; see Section 7)\n14: \n15: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n16: \n17: 1. No replacement server design; official surface proven usable.\n18: 2. No production mutation; research read-only.\n19: 3. No design judgment in the transport; sk-design is the taste authority.\n20: 4. No scope expansion into sibling integrations or generic MCP internals.\n21: 5. Evidence over assertion; unverifiable claims marked UNKNOWN.\n22: \n23: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n24: \n25: 1. Iteration cap reached (5) with max-iterations stop policy — SATISFIED (telemetry-only convergence, no early stop).\n26: 2. Lineage timeout — not triggered.\n27: 3. Contract rejection — not triggered.\n28: 4. Unsafe boundary — not triggered (research read-only; no credentials used).\n29: 5. Synthesis complete — SATISFIED (research/research.md written with all required coverage).\n30: \n31: ## 6. KNOWN CONTEXT\n32: \n33: - resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate\n34: - Official server: webflow/mcp-server (npm webflow-mcp-server 1.0.1); remote OAuth (mcp.webflow.com/sse, mcp-remote experimental) and local WEBFLOW_TOKEN modes; 18 tool modules; Bridge App only for canvas ops; plan-based rate limits (60/120 rpm, 1 publish/min); publish to webflow.io staging subdomain vs custom domains; scopes table; owner/admin-only authorization; hub transport-leaf layout.\n35: \n36: ## 7. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n37: \n38: - Q1: operation classes enumerated per module/action (research.md Section 4).\n39: - Q2: remote OAuth (experimental) + local bearer token (site/workspace/OAuth); no client-specific flow.\n40: - Q3: mcp-webflow is a TRANSPORT (hub leaf layout + mutations land in Webflow cloud).\n41: - Q4: dedicated test workspace + test site; read-only scopes baseline; staging-subdomain publish.\n42: - Q5: publish/destructive/deploy classes confirmation-gated; staged-first rollback; API restore UNKNOWN.\n43: - Q6: Designer-family ops pair with sk-design; Data-family ops do not.\n44: \n45: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n46: \n47: - GitHub API tree + per-module zod-schema extraction = authoritative action inventory.\n48: - Official docs .md suffix = clean markdown for citations.\n49: - Scopes + publish references made Q4/Q5 concrete.\n50: - Hub layout inspection grounded Q3 classification.\n51: \n52: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n53: \n54: - README `./tools` path stale (repo uses src/tools/).\n55: - Several guessed doc slugs 404; sitemap + llms.txt needed for discovery.\n56: - Single-page ai-tools doc hides per-section content behind JS; .md export fixed that.\n57: \n58: ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES\n59: \n60: - npm webflow-mcp as server package (third-party).\n61: - Workspace token as general write credential (no site scope).\n62: - API site duplication/backup for test scaffolding (not in API).\n63: - CMS mutations as implicitly draft-safe (live-site mutation possible).\n64: - mcp-webflow as a workflow system (transport executes; hub orchestrates).\n65: \n66: ## 11. RULED-OUT DIRECTIONS\n67: \n68: See Section 10 and research.md \"Eliminated Alternatives\".\n69: \n70: ## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n71: \n72: None — lineage complete. Handoff: research/research.md feeds the 015 packet's Phase 2 architecture/safety contract (permission surface, auth choice, confirmation/rollback policy).\n\n(End of file - total 72 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Deep Research Strategy - deepseek-max lineage\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nDetached fan-out lineage for the 015-mcp-webflow Phase 1 research run. Executor: cli-pi (deepseek-v4-flash). Stop policy: max-iterations (5), convergence off (telemetry only). Status: COMPLETE — synthesis written, config.status=complete.\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nWebflow MCP 2.0 — synthesize capabilities, constraints, and recommendations from official and corroborating sources.\n\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n\n(none — all six answered; see Section 7)\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n1. No replacement server design; official surface proven usable.\n2. No production mutation; research read-only.\n3. No design judgment in the transport; sk-design is the taste authority.\n4. No scope expansion into sibling integrations or generic MCP internals.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/deep-research-strategy.md","text":"# Deep Research Strategy - deepseek-max lineage\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nDetached fan-out lineage for the 015-mcp-webflow Phase 1 research run. Executor: cli-pi (deepseek-v4-flash). Stop policy: max-iterations (5), convergence off (telemetry only). Status: COMPLETE — synthesis written, config.status=complete.\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nWebflow MCP 2.0 — synthesize capabilities, constraints, and recommendations from official and corroborating sources.\n\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n\n(none — all six answered; see Section 7)\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n1. No replacement server design; official surface proven usable.\n2. No production mutation; research read-only.\n3. No design judgment in the transport; sk-design is the taste authority.\n4. No scope expansion into sibling integrations or generic MCP internals.\n5. Evidence over assertion; unverifiable claims marked UNKNOWN.\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n1. Iteration cap reached (5) with max-iterations stop policy — SATISFIED (telemetry-only convergence, no early stop).\n2. Lineage timeout — not triggered.\n3. Contract rejection — not triggered.\n4. Unsafe boundary — not triggered (research read-only; no credentials used).\n5. Synthesis complete — SATISFIED (research/research.md written with all required coverage).\n\n## 6. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n- resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate\n- Official server: webflow/mcp-server (npm webflow-mcp-server 1.0.1); remote OAuth (mcp.webflow.com/sse, mcp-remote experimental) and local WEBFLOW_TOKEN modes; 18 tool modules; Bridge App only for canvas ops; plan-based rate limits (60/120 rpm, 1 publish/min); publish to webflow.io staging subdomain vs custom domains; scopes table; owner/admin-only authorization; hub transport-leaf layout.\n\n## 7. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n\n- Q1: operation classes enumerated per module/action (research.md Section 4).\n- Q2: remote OAuth (experimental) + local bearer token (site/workspace/OAuth); no client-specific flow.\n- Q3: mcp-webflow is a TRANSPORT (hub leaf layout + mutations land in Webflow cloud).\n- Q4: dedicated test workspace + test site; read-only scopes baseline; staging-subdomain publish.\n- Q5: publish/destructive/deploy classes confirmation-gated; staged-first rollback; API restore UNKNOWN.\n- Q6: Designer-family ops pair with sk-design; Data-family ops do not.\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- GitHub API tree + per-module zod-schema extraction = authoritative action inventory.\n- Official docs .md suffix = clean markdown for citations.\n- Scopes + publish references made Q4/Q5 concrete.\n- Hub layout inspection grounded Q3 classification.\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- README `./tools` path stale (repo uses src/tools/).\n- Several guessed doc slugs 404; sitemap + llms.txt needed for discovery.\n- Single-page ai-tools doc hides per-section content behind JS; .md export fixed that.\n\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES\n\n- npm webflow-mcp as server package (third-party).\n- Workspace token as general write credential (no site scope).\n- API site duplication/backup for test scaffolding (not in API).\n- CMS mutations as implicitly draft-safe (live-site mutation possible).\n- mcp-webflow as a workflow system (transport executes; hub orchestrates).\n\n## 11. RULED-OUT DIRECTIONS\n\nSee Section 10 and research.md \"Eliminated Alternatives\".\n\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n\nNone — lineage complete. Handoff: research/research.md feeds the 015 packet's Phase 2 architecture/safety contract (permission surface, auth choice, confirmation/rollback policy).","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":72,"totalLines":72,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/deep-research-strategy.md","time":{"start":1785692184153,"end":1785692184175}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0e82b5215f04ee4c016a6f801804d4819191d40770d911f373"}},"id":"prt_fc38c5e530013Yoh7BlWl1FQ3N","sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","messageID":"msg_fc38c311c001q7qttDE6L1zQl8"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1785692186009,"sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","part":{"id":"prt_fc38c6592001vDUD4DlpuHsMUP","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","messageID":"msg_fc38c311c001q7qttDE6L1zQl8","sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":200722,"input":1102,"output":287,"reasoning":165,"cache":{"write":0,"read":199168}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1785692190046,"sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","part":{"id":"prt_fc38c755c0013S6RhlA8exm9iX","messageID":"msg_fc38c6b3d0014crYEO9Feu02II","sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785692196296,"sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_jW1kDBoxwTWkXzKL5rkbNqhD","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/research.md","limit":40},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/research.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Research Synthesis: Webflow MCP 2.0 (deepseek-max lineage)\n2: \n3: > Detached fan-out lineage of the 015-mcp-webflow Phase 1 deep research. Executor: cli-pi (deepseek-v4-flash). Stop policy: max-iterations (5); convergence off (telemetry only). All claims carry official-source citations or explicit inference markers.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Executive Summary\n6: \n7: Webflow MCP 2.0 is an official, actively maintained MCP server (`webflow/mcp-server`, npm `webflow-mcp-server@1.0.1`) exposing Webflow's Data API v2 and Designer API as MCP tools. It supports two connection modes — remote OAuth (`https://mcp.webflow.com/sse`, experimental `mcp-remote` transport) and local bearer token (`WEBFLOW_TOKEN`) — with a Designer \"Bridge App\" companion required only for canvas-bound operations. The surface is a bounded tool set (18 tool modules, combined-tool pattern with per-action schemas), not an API passthrough. Operations classify cleanly into read-only, draft-safe, destructive, publish-capable, and deployment-capable buckets, with publishing always an explicit separate action and rate limits per plan (60/120 rpm, 1 publish/min). For the mcp-tooling hub, `mcp-webflow` is a **transport** (mutations land in Webflow's cloud), registered as a transport leaf, with `sk-design` owning all design judgment.\n8: \n9: ## 2. Research Questions\n10: \n11: | ID | Question | Status |\n12: |----|----------|--------|\n13: | Q1 | Which MCP 2.0 actions are read-only, draft-safe, destructive, publish-capable, or deployment-capable? | **Answered** (Section 4) |\n14: | Q2 | Does the official surface use remote OAuth, a local server, an API token, or a client-specific connection flow? | **Answered** (Section 5) |\n15: | Q3 | Is `mcp-webflow` a `workflow` or a `transport`? | **Answered** (Section 9) |\n16: | Q4 | What non-production Webflow workspace or site can support live smoke? | **Answered** (Section 7) |\n17: | Q5 | Which Webflow operations require explicit operator confirmation, and which require a named rollback? | **Answered** (Section 8) |\n18: | Q6 | Which operations must pair with `sk-design` design judgment? | **Answered** (Section 10) |\n19: \n20: ## 3. Methodology\n21: \n22: Five iterations: (1) official surface inventory (announcement blog, README, package.json, GitHub tree); (2) per-module action extraction from server source (`src/tools/*.ts`) with HTTP-method classification; (3) authentication and rate-limit references; (4) scopes reference and publish semantics; (5) classification, confirmation policy, and integration recommendation grounded in the mcp-tooling hub layout. All sources official (webflow.com, developers.webflow.com, github.com/webflow/mcp-server).\n23: \n24: ## 4. Tool Inventory and Operation Classes (Q1)\n25: \n26: Combined-tool pattern: one MCP tool per module with an `actions` array; `annotations.readOnlyHint` exists only at tool level (`false` on all combined tools; `true` on `element_snapshot_tool`), so per-action classes derive from underlying HTTP method + payload.\n27: \n28: | Module (tool) | Read-only | Draft-safe mutation | Destructive | Publish-capable | Deployment-capable |\n29: |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n30: | pages (`data_pages_tool`) | `list_pages`, `get_page_metadata`, `get_page_content` | `update_page_settings` (draft settings; payload may flip publishing status) | — | `update_page_settings` (status field) | — |\n31: | cms (`data_cms_tool`) | `get_collection_list`, `get_collection_details`, `list_collection_items` | `create_collection`, `create_collection_*_field`, `update_collection_field`, `create_collection_items`, `update_collection_items` | `delete_collection_items` | `publish_collection_items` | — |\n32: | sites (`data_sites_tool`) | `list_sites`, `get_site` | — | — | `publish_site` | — |\n33: | workflows (`data_workflows_tool`) | `list_workflows`, `list_workflow_runs`, `get_workflow_run` | — | — | — | `run_workflow` |\n34: | scripts (`data_scripts_tool`) | `list_registered_scripts`, `list_applied_scripts`, `get_page_script` | `add_inline_site_script`, `upsert_page_script` | `delete_all_site_scripts`, `delete_all_page_scripts` | — | script registration ships with site publish |\n35: | components (`data_components_tool`) | `list_components`, `get_component_content`, `get_component_properties` | `update_component_content`, `update_component_properties` | — | — | — |\n36: | dePages (`de_page_tool`) | — | `create_page`, `create_page_folder`, `switch_page` | — | — | — |\n37: | deElement (`element_tool`/`element_snapshot_tool`) | `query_elements`, `get_selected_element`, snapshot tool | `select_element`, `set_text`, `set_style`, `set_link`, `set_heading_level`, `set_image_asset`, `add_or_update_attribute`, `update_id_attribute` | `remove_element`, `remove_attribute` | — | — |\n38: | deVariable (`variable_tool`) | `get_variable_collections`, `get_variables`, `query_variables` | `create_variable_collection`, `create_variable_mode`, `create_*_variable`, `update_*_variable`, `rename_variable` | `delete_variable` | — | — |\n39: | Not inspected (source-verified existence only) | aiChat, comments, enterprise, rules, webhooks, localDeMCPConnection | | | | |\n40: \n\n(Showing lines 1-40 of 115. Use offset=41 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Research Synthesis: Webflow MCP 2.0 (deepseek-max lineage)\n\n> Detached fan-out lineage of the 015-mcp-webflow Phase 1 deep research. Executor: cli-pi (deepseek-v4-flash). Stop policy: max-iterations (5); convergence off (telemetry only). All claims carry official-source citations or explicit inference markers.\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nWebflow MCP 2.0 is an official, actively maintained MCP server (`webflow/mcp-server`, npm `webflow-mcp-server@1.0.1`) exposing Webflow's Data API v2 and Designer API as MCP tools. It supports two connection modes — remote OAuth (`https://mcp.webflow.com/sse`, experimental `mcp-remote` transport) and local bearer token (`WEBFLOW_TOKEN`) — with a Designer \"Bridge App\" companion required only for canvas-bound operations. The surface is a bounded tool set (18 tool modules, combined-tool pattern with per-action schemas), not an API passthrough. Operations classify cleanly into read-only, draft-safe, destructive, publish-capable, and deployment-capable buckets, with publishing always an explicit separate action and rate limits per plan (60/120 rpm, 1 publish/min). For the mcp-tooling hub, `mcp-webflow` is a **transport** (mutations land in Webflow's cloud), registered as a transport leaf, with `sk-design` owning all design judgment.\n\n## 2. Research Questions\n\n| ID | Question | Status |\n|----|----------|--------|\n| Q1 | Which MCP 2.0 actions are read-only, draft-safe, destructive, publish-capable, or deployment-capable? | **Answered** (Section 4) |\n| Q2 | Does the official surface use remote OAuth, a local server, an API token, or a client-specific connection flow? | **Answered** (Section 5) |\n| Q3 | Is `mcp-webflow` a `workflow` or a `transport`? | **Answered** (Section 9) |\n| Q4 | What non-production Webflow workspace or site can support live smoke? | **Answered** (Section 7) |\n| Q5 | Which Webflow operations require explicit operator confirmation, and which require a named rollback? | **Answered** (Section 8) |\n| Q6 | Which operations must pair with `sk-design` design judgment? | **Answered** (Section 10) |\n\n## 3. Methodology","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/research.md","text":"# Research Synthesis: Webflow MCP 2.0 (deepseek-max lineage)\n\n> Detached fan-out lineage of the 015-mcp-webflow Phase 1 deep research. Executor: cli-pi (deepseek-v4-flash). Stop policy: max-iterations (5); convergence off (telemetry only). All claims carry official-source citations or explicit inference markers.\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nWebflow MCP 2.0 is an official, actively maintained MCP server (`webflow/mcp-server`, npm `webflow-mcp-server@1.0.1`) exposing Webflow's Data API v2 and Designer API as MCP tools. It supports two connection modes — remote OAuth (`https://mcp.webflow.com/sse`, experimental `mcp-remote` transport) and local bearer token (`WEBFLOW_TOKEN`) — with a Designer \"Bridge App\" companion required only for canvas-bound operations. The surface is a bounded tool set (18 tool modules, combined-tool pattern with per-action schemas), not an API passthrough. Operations classify cleanly into read-only, draft-safe, destructive, publish-capable, and deployment-capable buckets, with publishing always an explicit separate action and rate limits per plan (60/120 rpm, 1 publish/min). For the mcp-tooling hub, `mcp-webflow` is a **transport** (mutations land in Webflow's cloud), registered as a transport leaf, with `sk-design` owning all design judgment.\n\n## 2. Research Questions\n\n| ID | Question | Status |\n|----|----------|--------|\n| Q1 | Which MCP 2.0 actions are read-only, draft-safe, destructive, publish-capable, or deployment-capable? | **Answered** (Section 4) |\n| Q2 | Does the official surface use remote OAuth, a local server, an API token, or a client-specific connection flow? | **Answered** (Section 5) |\n| Q3 | Is `mcp-webflow` a `workflow` or a `transport`? | **Answered** (Section 9) |\n| Q4 | What non-production Webflow workspace or site can support live smoke? | **Answered** (Section 7) |\n| Q5 | Which Webflow operations require explicit operator confirmation, and which require a named rollback? | **Answered** (Section 8) |\n| Q6 | Which operations must pair with `sk-design` design judgment? | **Answered** (Section 10) |\n\n## 3. Methodology\n\nFive iterations: (1) official surface inventory (announcement blog, README, package.json, GitHub tree); (2) per-module action extraction from server source (`src/tools/*.ts`) with HTTP-method classification; (3) authentication and rate-limit references; (4) scopes reference and publish semantics; (5) classification, confirmation policy, and integration recommendation grounded in the mcp-tooling hub layout. All sources official (webflow.com, developers.webflow.com, github.com/webflow/mcp-server).\n\n## 4. Tool Inventory and Operation Classes (Q1)\n\nCombined-tool pattern: one MCP tool per module with an `actions` array; `annotations.readOnlyHint` exists only at tool level (`false` on all combined tools; `true` on `element_snapshot_tool`), so per-action classes derive from underlying HTTP method + payload.\n\n| Module (tool) | Read-only | Draft-safe mutation | Destructive | Publish-capable | Deployment-capable |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| pages (`data_pages_tool`) | `list_pages`, `get_page_metadata`, `get_page_content` | `update_page_settings` (draft settings; payload may flip publishing status) | — | `update_page_settings` (status field) | — |\n| cms (`data_cms_tool`) | `get_collection_list`, `get_collection_details`, `list_collection_items` | `create_collection`, `create_collection_*_field`, `update_collection_field`, `create_collection_items`, `update_collection_items` | `delete_collection_items` | `publish_collection_items` | — |\n| sites (`data_sites_tool`) | `list_sites`, `get_site` | — | — | `publish_site` | — |\n| workflows (`data_workflows_tool`) | `list_workflows`, `list_workflow_runs`, `get_workflow_run` | — | — | — | `run_workflow` |\n| scripts (`data_scripts_tool`) | `list_registered_scripts`, `list_applied_scripts`, `get_page_script` | `add_inline_site_script`, `upsert_page_script` | `delete_all_site_scripts`, `delete_all_page_scripts` | — | script registration ships with site publish |\n| components (`data_components_tool`) | `list_components`, `get_component_content`, `get_component_properties` | `update_component_content`, `update_component_properties` | — | — | — |\n| dePages (`de_page_tool`) | — | `create_page`, `create_page_folder`, `switch_page` | — | — | — |\n| deElement (`element_tool`/`element_snapshot_tool`) | `query_elements`, `get_selected_element`, snapshot tool | `select_element`, `set_text`, `set_style`, `set_link`, `set_heading_level`, `set_image_asset`, `add_or_update_attribute`, `update_id_attribute` | `remove_element`, `remove_attribute` | — | — |\n| deVariable (`variable_tool`) | `get_variable_collections`, `get_variables`, `query_variables` | `create_variable_collection`, `create_variable_mode`, `create_*_variable`, `update_*_variable`, `rename_variable` | `delete_variable` | — | — |\n| Not inspected (source-verified existence only) | aiChat, comments, enterprise, rules, webhooks, localDeMCPConnection | | | | |\n","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":40,"totalLines":115,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/research.md","time":{"start":1785692196281,"end":1785692196294}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_093828bc021ec3f5016a6f80241de88191a4d45755abf75f78"}},"id":"prt_fc38c8d68001n3vunyXYGu6XEH","sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","messageID":"msg_fc38c6b3d0014crYEO9Feu02II"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785692196308,"sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_TwxdDApsstJqRiLxOP1ZrwMm","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/resource-map.md","limit":20},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/resource-map.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Resource Map (evidence-derived) — Webflow MCP 2.0 lineage\n2: \n3: Generated from converged deltas. Categories: official documentation, official server source, repository surfaces.\n4: \n5: ## Documents\n6: \n7: | Resource | Type | Theme |\n8: |----------|------|-------|\n9: | https://webflow.com/blog/mcp-2-features | Official announcement | MCP 2.0 capabilities: components, CSS variables, agent instructions, analytics |\n10: | https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md | Official docs | MCP server overview, limitations, installation, FAQs |\n11: | https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/authentication.md | Official docs | Token types: site, workspace, OAuth |\n12: | https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/scopes.md | Official docs | Site-level and workspace-level permission scopes |\n13: | https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/authentication/site-token.md | Official docs | Site token creation, minimal-scope practice |\n14: | https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/authentication/workspace-token.md | Official docs | Workspace token limits (no site scope) |\n15: | https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rate-limits.md | Official docs | Plan-based rate limits, 429 handling, headers |\n16: | https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/sites/publish.md | Official docs | Publish endpoint: staging subdomain vs custom domains, 1/min |\n17: | https://developers.webflow.com/llms.txt | Official index | LLM-readable docs index |\n18: \n19: ## Commands\n20: \n\n(Showing lines 1-20 of 37. Use offset=21 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Resource Map (evidence-derived) — Webflow MCP 2.0 lineage\n\nGenerated from converged deltas. Categories: official documentation, official server source, repository surfaces.\n\n## Documents\n\n| Resource | Type | Theme |\n|----------|------|-------|\n| https://webflow.com/blog/mcp-2-features | Official announcement | MCP 2.0 capabilities: components, CSS variables, agent instructions, analytics |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md | Official docs | MCP server overview, limitations, installation, FAQs |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/authentication.md | Official docs | Token types: site, workspace, OAuth |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/scopes.md | Official docs | Site-level and workspace-level permission scopes |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/authentication/site-token.md | Official docs | Site token creation, minimal-scope practice |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/authentication/workspace-token.md | Official docs | Workspace token limits (no site scope) |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rate-limits.md | Official docs | Plan-based rate limits, 429 handling, headers |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/sites/publish.md | Official docs | Publish endpoint: staging subdomain vs custom domains, 1/min |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/llms.txt | Official index | LLM-readable docs index |\n\n## Commands\n","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/resource-map.md","text":"# Resource Map (evidence-derived) — Webflow MCP 2.0 lineage\n\nGenerated from converged deltas. Categories: official documentation, official server source, repository surfaces.\n\n## Documents\n\n| Resource | Type | Theme |\n|----------|------|-------|\n| https://webflow.com/blog/mcp-2-features | Official announcement | MCP 2.0 capabilities: components, CSS variables, agent instructions, analytics |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md | Official docs | MCP server overview, limitations, installation, FAQs |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/authentication.md | Official docs | Token types: site, workspace, OAuth |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/scopes.md | Official docs | Site-level and workspace-level permission scopes |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/authentication/site-token.md | Official docs | Site token creation, minimal-scope practice |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/authentication/workspace-token.md | Official docs | Workspace token limits (no site scope) |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rate-limits.md | Official docs | Plan-based rate limits, 429 handling, headers |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/sites/publish.md | Official docs | Publish endpoint: staging subdomain vs custom domains, 1/min |\n| https://developers.webflow.com/llms.txt | Official index | LLM-readable docs index |\n\n## Commands\n","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":20,"totalLines":37,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek-max/resource-map.md","time":{"start":1785692196301,"end":1785692196306}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_093828bc021ec3f5016a6f80241e0c8191b7df755b0f267697"}},"id":"prt_fc38c8dbd0017HQ1JPPOkgkiIS","sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","messageID":"msg_fc38c6b3d0014crYEO9Feu02II"}}
