{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785692622194,"sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_jDk2ePJinKTLh8VBEw4SjckH","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/luna-fast/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/luna-fast/deep-research-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deep Research Strategy - luna-fast lineage\n2: \n3: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n4: \n5: Detached fan-out lineage for the 015-mcp-webflow Phase 1 research run. Executor: cli-opencode (openai/gpt-5.6-luna-fast, xhigh). Stop policy: max-iterations (5), convergence off (telemetry only). All artifacts are confined to this lineage directory.\n6: \n7: ## 2. TOPIC\n8: \n9: Webflow MCP 2.0 features, followed by official Webflow MCP, developer, API, authentication, and changelog documentation.\n10: \n11: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n12: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n13: - [x] Q1: What did the MCP 2.0 announcement add, and which claims are confirmed by official implementation or developer docs?\n14: - [ ] Q2: What is the official MCP server surface, transport, client setup, and supported capability boundary?\n15: - [ ] Q3: What authentication, OAuth, token, scope, role, and secret-handling rules apply?\n16: - [ ] Q4: What operational constraints exist for rate limits, pagination, errors, retries, publishing, and changelog evolution?\n17: - [ ] Q5: What safe integration and confirmation model follows for mcp-tooling, including sk-design pairing?\n18: \n19: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n20: \n21: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n22: \n23: 1. No tool installation, registration, or repository implementation.\n24: 2. No Webflow create, update, delete, publish, deploy, or other mutating calls.\n25: 3. No credentials, tokens, private site data, or production connections.\n26: 4. No unsupported capability claims based only on marketing language.\n27: 5. No edits outside this detached lineage directory.\n28: \n29: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n30: \n31: 1. Run exactly five evidence-gathering iterations; convergence is telemetry only.\n32: 2. Stop early only for an unrecoverable state or safety failure, not low novelty.\n33: 3. Synthesis must preserve source citations, contradictions, negative knowledge, and open questions.\n34: 4. Resource map and final synthesis must be written inside this lineage directory.\n35: \n36: ## 6. KNOWN CONTEXT\n37: \n38: - resource-map.md not present at init; skipping pre-existing resource-map coverage gate.\n39: - The sibling deepseek-max lineage is a separate evidence stream and is not treated as authoritative for this lineage.\n40: - Required starting source: https://webflow.com/blog/mcp-2-features\n41: - Official documentation families to follow: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools, https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference, https://developers.webflow.com/changelog, and the official https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server repository.\n42: \n43: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n44: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n45: - Q1: What did the MCP 2.0 announcement add, and which claims are confirmed by official implementation or developer docs?\n46: \n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n48: \n49: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n50: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n51: - Fetching the supplied announcement alongside the current MCP “How it works” page, AI-tools page, and official repository separated marketing-level claims from documented capability boundaries. (iteration 1)\n52: \n53: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n54: \n55: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n56: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n57: - The repository landing page was too high-level to confirm individual MCP 2.0 tools; it links to the tool directory without presenting that inventory inline. (iteration 1)\n58: \n59: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n60: \n61: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n62: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n63: ### Calling Webflow MCP mutation tools was not attempted because the prompt explicitly forbids tool invocation; therefore no runtime mutation evidence was collected. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n64: - What was tried: Calling Webflow MCP mutation tools was not attempted because the prompt explicitly forbids tool invocation; therefore no runtime mutation evidence was collected.\n65: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n66: - Do NOT retry: Calling Webflow MCP mutation tools was not attempted because the prompt explicitly forbids tool invocation; therefore no runtime mutation evidence was collected.\n67: \n68: ### Client setup, authentication, transport, rate limits, and safe integration design were deferred because they are separate strategy questions rather than this iteration's announcement-confirmation focus. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n69: - What was tried: Client setup, authentication, transport, rate limits, and safe integration design were deferred because they are separate strategy questions rather than this iteration's announcement-confirmation focus.\n70: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n71: - Do NOT retry: Client setup, authentication, transport, rate limits, and safe integration design were deferred because they are separate strategy questions rather than this iteration's announcement-confirmation focus.\n72: \n73: ### Non-official articles, community reports, and broad implementation research were excluded to preserve the supplied official-primary-source scope. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n74: - What was tried: Non-official articles, community reports, and broad implementation research were excluded to preserve the supplied official-primary-source scope.\n75: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n76: - Do NOT retry: Non-official articles, community reports, and broad implementation research were excluded to preserve the supplied official-primary-source scope.\n77: \n78: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n79: \n80: <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n81: ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n82: - Calling Webflow MCP mutation tools was not attempted because the prompt explicitly forbids tool invocation; therefore no runtime mutation evidence was collected. (iteration 1)\n83: - Client setup, authentication, transport, rate limits, and safe integration design were deferred because they are separate strategy questions rather than this iteration's announcement-confirmation focus. (iteration 1)\n84: - Non-official articles, community reports, and broad implementation research were excluded to preserve the supplied official-primary-source scope. (iteration 1)\n85: \n86: <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n87: \n88: <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n89: ## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n90: - Completed pivots: 0\n91: - Failed pivots: 0\n92: - Audited overrides: 0\n93: - Saturated: none yet\n94: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n95: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n96: \n97: <!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n98: \n99: <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n100: ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n101: [None yet]\n102: \n103: <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n104: \n105: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n106: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n107: Follow up on: Several “more to offer” claims remain unverified by the official primary sources fetched in this iteration. The docs confirm broad Data API coverage and list CMS, assets, pages, custom code, localization, and Designer...\n108: \n109: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n(End of file - total 109 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Deep Research Strategy - luna-fast lineage\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nDetached fan-out lineage for the 015-mcp-webflow Phase 1 research run. Executor: cli-opencode (openai/gpt-5.6-luna-fast, xhigh). Stop policy: max-iterations (5), convergence off (telemetry only). All artifacts are confined to this lineage directory.\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nWebflow MCP 2.0 features, followed by official Webflow MCP, developer, API, authentication, and changelog documentation.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [x] Q1: What did the MCP 2.0 announcement add, and which claims are confirmed by official implementation or developer docs?\n- [ ] Q2: What is the official MCP server surface, transport, client setup, and supported capability boundary?\n- [ ] Q3: What authentication, OAuth, token, scope, role, and secret-handling rules apply?\n- [ ] Q4: What operational constraints exist for rate limits, pagination, errors, retries, publishing, and changelog evolution?\n- [ ] Q5: What safe integration and confirmation model follows for mcp-tooling, including sk-design pairing?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/luna-fast/deep-research-strategy.md","text":"# Deep Research Strategy - luna-fast lineage\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nDetached fan-out lineage for the 015-mcp-webflow Phase 1 research run. Executor: cli-opencode (openai/gpt-5.6-luna-fast, xhigh). Stop policy: max-iterations (5), convergence off (telemetry only). All artifacts are confined to this lineage directory.\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nWebflow MCP 2.0 features, followed by official Webflow MCP, developer, API, authentication, and changelog documentation.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [x] Q1: What did the MCP 2.0 announcement add, and which claims are confirmed by official implementation or developer docs?\n- [ ] Q2: What is the official MCP server surface, transport, client setup, and supported capability boundary?\n- [ ] Q3: What authentication, OAuth, token, scope, role, and secret-handling rules apply?\n- [ ] Q4: What operational constraints exist for rate limits, pagination, errors, retries, publishing, and changelog evolution?\n- [ ] Q5: What safe integration and confirmation model follows for mcp-tooling, including sk-design pairing?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n1. No tool installation, registration, or repository implementation.\n2. No Webflow create, update, delete, publish, deploy, or other mutating calls.\n3. No credentials, tokens, private site data, or production connections.\n4. No unsupported capability claims based only on marketing language.\n5. No edits outside this detached lineage directory.\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n1. Run exactly five evidence-gathering iterations; convergence is telemetry only.\n2. Stop early only for an unrecoverable state or safety failure, not low novelty.\n3. Synthesis must preserve source citations, contradictions, negative knowledge, and open questions.\n4. Resource map and final synthesis must be written inside this lineage directory.\n\n## 6. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n- resource-map.md not present at init; skipping pre-existing resource-map coverage gate.\n- The sibling deepseek-max lineage is a separate evidence stream and is not treated as authoritative for this lineage.\n- Required starting source: https://webflow.com/blog/mcp-2-features\n- Official documentation families to follow: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools, https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference, https://developers.webflow.com/changelog, and the official https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server repository.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n- Q1: What did the MCP 2.0 announcement add, and which claims are confirmed by official implementation or developer docs?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n- Fetching the supplied announcement alongside the current MCP “How it works” page, AI-tools page, and official repository separated marketing-level claims from documented capability boundaries. (iteration 1)\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n- The repository landing page was too high-level to confirm individual MCP 2.0 tools; it links to the tool directory without presenting that inventory inline. (iteration 1)\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n### Calling Webflow MCP mutation tools was not attempted because the prompt explicitly forbids tool invocation; therefore no runtime mutation evidence was collected. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n- What was tried: Calling Webflow MCP mutation tools was not attempted because the prompt explicitly forbids tool invocation; therefore no runtime mutation evidence was collected.\n- Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n- Do NOT retry: Calling Webflow MCP mutation tools was not attempted because the prompt explicitly forbids tool invocation; therefore no runtime mutation evidence was collected.\n\n### Client setup, authentication, transport, rate limits, and safe integration design were deferred because they are separate strategy questions rather than this iteration's announcement-confirmation focus. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n- What was tried: Client setup, authentication, transport, rate limits, and safe integration design were deferred because they are separate strategy questions rather than this iteration's announcement-confirmation focus.\n- Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n- Do NOT retry: Client setup, authentication, transport, rate limits, and safe integration design were deferred because they are separate strategy questions rather than this iteration's announcement-confirmation focus.\n\n### Non-official articles, community reports, and broad implementation research were excluded to preserve the supplied official-primary-source scope. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n- What was tried: Non-official articles, community reports, and broad implementation research were excluded to preserve the supplied official-primary-source scope.\n- Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n- Do NOT retry: Non-official articles, community reports, and broad implementation research were excluded to preserve the supplied official-primary-source scope.\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n- Calling Webflow MCP mutation tools was not attempted because the prompt explicitly forbids tool invocation; therefore no runtime mutation evidence was collected. (iteration 1)\n- Client setup, authentication, transport, rate limits, and safe integration design were deferred because they are separate strategy questions rather than this iteration's announcement-confirmation focus. (iteration 1)\n- Non-official articles, community reports, and broad implementation research were excluded to preserve the supplied official-primary-source scope. (iteration 1)\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[None yet]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nFollow up on: Several “more to offer” claims remain unverified by the official primary sources fetched in this iteration. The docs confirm broad Data API coverage and list CMS, assets, pages, custom code, localization, and Designer...\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":109,"totalLines":109,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/luna-fast/deep-research-strategy.md","time":{"start":1785692622178,"end":1785692622192}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_017cb3b50953e777016a6f81ce01c08191be922129de82f5ab"}},"id":"prt_fc3930d13001AnrwQSMX36TyYf","sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","messageID":"msg_fc392df7d001qerikcTTF3XUP8"}}
