gs: 5\n38: - openQuestions: 4\n39: - resolvedQuestions: 1\n40: \n41: <!-- /ANCHOR:progress -->\n42: <!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n43: ## 4. QUESTIONS\n44: - Answered: 1/5\n45: - [x] Q1: What did the MCP 2.0 announcement add, and which claims are confirmed by official implementation or developer docs?\n46: - [ ] Q2: What is the official MCP server surface, transport, client setup, and supported capability boundary? [legacy-import]\n47: - [ ] Q3: What authentication, OAuth, token, scope, role, and secret-handling rules apply? [legacy-import]\n48: - [ ] Q4: What operational constraints exist for rate limits, pagination, errors, retries, publishing, and changelog evolution? [legacy-import]\n49: - [ ] Q5: What safe integration and confirmation model follows for mcp-tooling, including sk-design pairing? [legacy-import]\n50: \n51: <!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n52: <!-- ANCHOR:uncovered-questions -->\n53: ## Uncovered Questions\n54: - Count: 4\n55: - [ ] Q2: What is the official MCP server surface, transport, client setup, and supported capability boundary?\n56: - [ ] Q3: What authentication, OAuth, token, scope, role, and secret-handling rules apply?\n57: - [ ] Q4: What operational constraints exist for rate limits, pagination, errors, retries, publishing, and changelog evolution?\n58: - [ ] Q5: What safe integration and confirmation model follows for mcp-tooling, including sk-design pairing?\n59: \n60: <!-- /ANCHOR:uncovered-questions -->\n61: <!-- ANCHOR:trend -->\n62: ## 5. TREND\n63: - newInfoRatio sparkline: ▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄\n64: - score sparkline: ▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄▄\n65: - Last 3 ratios: 0.80\n66: - Stuck count: 0\n67: - Guard violations: none recorded by the reducer pass\n68: - convergenceScore: 0.80\n69: - coverageBySources: {\"developers.webflow.com\":2,\"github.com\":1,\"webflow.com\":1}\n70: - Advisory events: none\n71: \n72: <!-- /ANCHOR:trend -->\n73: <!-- ANCHOR:dead-ends -->\n74: ## 6. DEAD ENDS\n75: - Calling Webflow MCP mutation tools was not attempted be