antics in consulted official references]\"]}\n6: {\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":4,\"id\":\"finding-4-5-publishing-boundary\",\"classification\":\"new\",\"text\":\"Site publishing requires sites:write, has explicit domain/page inputs, returns 202 when accepted, and is limited to one successful publish queue per minute.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/working-with-the-cms/manage-collections-and-items.md\"]}\n7: {\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":4,\"id\":\"finding-4-6-changelog-breaking-evolution\",\"classification\":\"new\",\"text\":\"The July 27 translatable=true contract was changed on July 29 to a secondary-locale ID with breaking 400 behavior for booleans and additional 403/500 cases.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/27.md\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/29.md\"]}\n8: {\"type\":\"invariant\",\"iteration\":4,\"text\":\"No Webflow MCP tools, credentials, or mutating calls were used.\",\"source\":\"dispatch constraints and execution record\"}\n9: {\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"iteration\":4,\"text\":\"Guessed standalone pagination and errors URLs were unavailable; official linked documentation was used instead.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/pagination\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/errors\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rest-introduction.md\"]}\n\n(End of file - total 9 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":4,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":4,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Official rate limits, pagination, errors, retries, publishing constraints, and changelog evolution\",\"findingsCount\":6,\"newInfoRatio\":1.0,\"noveltyJustification\":\"All six findings add new official operational or change-history evidence beyond the prior authentication and MCP-surface iterations.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Q4: What operational constraints exist for rate limits, pagination, errors, retries, publishing, and changelog evolution?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Q4 substantially answered for documented rate limits, offset pagination, error schema, retry guidance, publishing gates, and recent changelog evolution; idempotency guarantees remain undocumented\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Guessed standalone pagination and errors URLs returned Page Not Found; official REST introduction, error-handling, and CMS workflow pages were used instead\",\"Webflow MCP tool invocation, credentials, and mutating calls\"],\"focusTrack\":\"operational-constraints\",\"edgeCase\":\"partial-success\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"WebFetch\",\"Glob\",\"apply_patch\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rate-limits\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/error-handling.md\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rest-introduction.md\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/working-with-the-cms/manage-collections-and-items.md\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/27.md\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/29.md\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/llms.txt\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-02T18:05:00Z\",\"durationMs\":180000,\"graphEvents\":[]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":4,\"id\":\"finding-4-1-rate-limits-and-headers\",\"classification\":\"new\",\"text\":\"Plan-based request ceilings, rate headers, per-key accounting, and endpoint-specific limits are documented.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rate-limits\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":4,\"id\":\"finding-4-2-cms-offset-pagination\",\"classification\":\"new\",\"text\":\"CMS collection-item listing uses limit up to 100, offset, and pagination.total/limit/offset.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/working-with-the-cms/manage-collections-and-items.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":4,\"id\":\"finding-4-3-error-contract\",\"classification\":\"new\",\"text\":\"Errors use standard HTTP classes and a structured code/message/externalReference/details body.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/error-handling.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":4,\"id\":\"finding-4-4-retry-and-idempotency-gap\",\"classification\":\"new\",\"text\":\"SDK exponential backoff and Retry-After are documented; idempotency keys and replay guarantees were not documented in the consulted official sources.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/error-handling.md\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rate-limits\",\"[INFERENCE: absence of idempotency-key and replay semantics in consulted official references]\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":4,\"id\":\"finding-4-5-publishing-boundary\",\"classification\":\"new\",\"text\":\"Site publishing requires sites:write, has explicit domain/page inputs, returns 202 when accepted, and is limited to one successful publish queue per minute.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/working-with-the-cms/manage-collections-and-items.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":4,\"id\":\"finding-4-6-changelog-breaking-evolution\",\"classification\":\"new\",\"text\":\"The July 27 translatable=true contract was changed on July 29 to a secondary-locale ID with breaking 400 behavior for booleans and additional 403/500 cases.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/27.md\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/29.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"invariant\",\"iteration\":4,\"text\":\"No Webflow MCP tools, credentials, or mutating calls were used.\",\"source\":\"dispatch constraints and execution record\"}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"iteration\":4,\"text\":\"Guessed standalone pagination and errors URLs were unavailable; official linked documentation was used instead.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/pagination\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/errors\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rest-introduction.md\"]}","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/luna-fast/deltas/iter-004.jsonl","text":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":4,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":4,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Official rate limits, pagination, errors, retries, publishing constraints, and changelog evolution\",\"findingsCount\":6,\"newInfoRatio\":1.0,\"noveltyJustification\":\"All six findings add new official operational or change-history evidence beyond the prior authentication and MCP-surface iterations.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Q4: What operational constraints exist for rate limits, pagination, errors, retries, publishing, and changelog evolution?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Q4 substantially answered for documented rate limits, offset pagination, error schema, retry guidance, publishing gates, and recent changelog evolution; idempotency guarantees remain undocumented\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Guessed standalone pagination and errors URLs returned Page Not Found; official REST introduction, error-handling, and CMS workflow pages were used instead\",\"Webflow MCP tool invocation, credentials, and mutating calls\"],\"focusTrack\":\"operational-constraints\",\"edgeCase\":\"partial-success\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"WebFetch\",\"Glob\",\"apply_patch\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rate-limits\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/error-handling.md\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rest-introduction.md\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/working-with-the-cms/manage-collections-and-items.md\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/27.md\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/29.md\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/llms.txt\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-02T18:05:00Z\",\"durationMs\":180000,\"graphEvents\":[]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":4,\"id\":\"finding-4-1-rate-limits-and-headers\",\"classification\":\"new\",\"text\":\"Plan-based request ceilings, rate headers, per-key accounting, and endpoint-specific limits are documented.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rate-limits\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":4,\"id\":\"finding-4-2-cms-offset-pagination\",\"classification\":\"new\",\"text\":\"CMS collection-item listing uses limit up to 100, offset, and pagination.total/limit/offset.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/working-with-the-cms/manage-collections-and-items.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":4,\"id\":\"finding-4-3-error-contract\",\"classification\":\"new\",\"text\":\"Errors use standard HTTP classes and a structured code/message/externalReference/details body.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/error-handling.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":4,\"id\":\"finding-4-4-retry-and-idempotency-gap\",\"classification\":\"new\",\"text\":\"SDK exponential backoff and Retry-After are documented; idempotency keys and replay guarantees were not documented in the consulted official sources.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/error-handling.md\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rate-limits\",\"[INFERENCE: absence of idempotency-key and replay semantics in consulted official references]\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":4,\"id\":\"finding-4-5-publishing-boundary\",\"classification\":\"new\",\"text\":\"Site publishing requires sites:write, has explicit domain/page inputs, returns 202 when accepted, and is limited to one successful publish queue per minute.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/working-with-the-cms/manage-collections-and-items.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":4,\"id\":\"finding-4-6-changelog-breaking-evolution\",\"classification\":\"new\",\"text\":\"The July 27 translatable=true contract was changed on July 29 to a secondary-locale ID with breaking 400 behavior for booleans and additional 403/500 cases.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/27.md\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/29.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"invariant\",\"iteration\":4,\"text\":\"No Webflow MCP tools, credentials, or mutating calls were used.\",\"source\":\"dispatch constraints and execution record\"}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"iteration\":4,\"text\":\"Guessed standalone pagination and errors URLs were unavailable; official linked documentation was used instead.\",\"sources\":[\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/pagination\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/errors\",\"https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rest-introduction.md\"]}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":9,"totalLines":9,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/luna-fast/deltas/iter-004.jsonl","time":{"start":1785694043428,"end":1785694043442}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0b231802796e93c5016a6f875a926c8191a721113e3f0eabfd"}},"id":"prt_fc3a8bcd8001wR3hW4eZBaHCSM","sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","messageID":"msg_fc3a89840001uI09CAituZq07G"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785694043539,"sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_OhidsXqoUCeoktdp3SzRmfzu","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/luna-fast/research.md","limit":100},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/luna-fast/research.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Research Synthesis\n2: \n3: ## Iteration 3: Authentication and authorization\n4: \n5: - Remote Webflow MCP uses OAuth, selected site/workspace authorization, automatic refresh, and no local API-key storage. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/reference/how-it-works.md]`\n6: - MCP access remains bounded by existing Webflow permissions and roles; site owners/admins authorize the server and each authorization covers one workspace. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]` `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/reference/overview.md]`\n7: - OAuth Data Client apps, site tokens, workspace tokens, and the official repository's local `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` stdio path are distinct credential/deployment models. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/oauth-app.md]` `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/authentication/site-token.md]` `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/authentication/workspace-token.md]` `[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]`\n8: - Scopes are resource-specific and should be minimized; OAuth install scopes must be registered, workspace tokens do not provide site scope, and site tokens cannot access custom-code endpoints. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/scopes.md]`\n9: - Official guidance supports secure storage, minimal scopes, rotation, and revocation. Webflow documents a Beta MCP server but no isolated staging sandbox or non-production credential class in the sources consulted. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/oauth-app.md]` `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/reference/getting-started.md]`\n10: \n11: ## Iteration 4: Operational constraints and changelog evolution\n12: \n13: - Data API limits are plan-based: 60 requests/minute for Starter/Basic, 120 for CMS/eCommerce/Business, and custom for Enterprise. Responses expose `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, `X-RateLimit-Limit`, and `Retry-After`; endpoint-specific limits can be stricter. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rate-limits]`\n14: - CMS collection-item listing uses offset pagination with a maximum `limit` of 100 and a `pagination` object containing `total`, `limit`, and `offset`; this is endpoint-scoped evidence, not a universal claim. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/working-with-the-cms/manage-collections-and-items.md]`\n15: - Errors use standard HTTP classes and a structured `code`/`message`/`externalReference`/`details` response. SDKs provide exponential backoff and custom clients should honor `Retry-After`; no idempotency-key or replay guarantee was documented in the consulted official references. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/error-handling.md]` `[INFERENCE: absence of idempotency-key and replay semantics in consulted official references]`\n16: - Publishing requires `sites:write`, explicit domain or Webflow-subdomain inputs, and is limited to one successful publish queue per minute; staging-to-production publishing can include all staged changes. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish]`\n17: - Webflow changed the `translatable` parameter from boolean semantics on July 27 to a target secondary-locale ID on July 29, making booleans return 400 and adding documented 403/500 cases. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/27.md]` `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/29.md]`\n\n(End of file - total 17 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Research Synthesis\n\n## Iteration 3: Authentication and authorization\n\n- Remote Webflow MCP uses OAuth, selected site/workspace authorization, automatic refresh, and no local API-key storage. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/reference/how-it-works.md]`\n- MCP access remains bounded by existing Webflow permissions and roles; site owners/admins authorize the server and each authorization covers one workspace. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]` `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/reference/overview.md]`\n- OAuth Data Client apps, site tokens, workspace tokens, and the official repository's local `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` stdio path are distinct credential/deployment models. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/oauth-app.md]` `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/authentication/site-token.md]` `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/authentication/workspace-token.md]` `[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]`\n- Scopes are resource-specific and should be minimized; OAuth install scopes must be registered, workspace tokens do not provide site scope, and site tokens cannot access custom-code endpoints. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/scopes.md]`\n- Official guidance supports secure storage, minimal scopes, rotation, and revocation. Webflow documents a Beta MCP server but no isolated staging sandbox or non-production credential class in the sources consulted. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/oauth-app.md]` `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/reference/getting-started.md]`\n\n## Iteration 4: Operational constraints and changelog evolution\n\n- Data API limits are plan-based: 60 requests/minute for Starter/Basic, 120 for CMS/eCommerce/Business, and custom for Enterprise. Responses expose `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, `X-RateLimit-Limit`, and `Retry-After`; endpoint-specific limits can be stricter. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rate-limits]`\n- CMS collection-item listing uses offset pagination with a maximum `limit` of 100 and a `pagination` object containing `total`, `limit`, and `offset`; this is endpoint-scoped evidence, not a universal claim. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/working-with-the-cms/manage-collections-and-items.md]`\n- Errors use standard HTTP classes and a structured `code`/`message`/`externalReference`/`details` response. SDKs provide exponential backoff and custom clients should honor `Retry-After`; no idempotency-key or replay guarantee was documented in the consulted official references. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/error-handling.md]` `[INFERENCE: absence of idempotency-key and replay semantics in consulted official references]`\n- Publishing requires `sites:write`, explicit domain or Webflow-subdomain inputs, and is limited to one successful publish queue per minute; staging-to-production publishing can include all staged changes. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish]`\n- Webflow changed the `translatable` parameter from boolean semantics on July 27 to a target secondary-locale ID on July 29, making booleans return 400 and adding documented 403/500 cases. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/27.md]` `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/29.md]`","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/luna-fast/research.md","text":"# Research Synthesis\n\n## Iteration 3: Authentication and authorization\n\n- Remote Webflow MCP uses OAuth, selected site/workspace authorization, automatic refresh, and no local API-key storage. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/reference/how-it-works.md]`\n- MCP access remains bounded by existing Webflow permissions and roles; site owners/admins authorize the server and each authorization covers one workspace. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/ai-tools.md]` `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/reference/overview.md]`\n- OAuth Data Client apps, site tokens, workspace tokens, and the official repository's local `WEBFLOW_TOKEN` stdio path are distinct credential/deployment models. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/oauth-app.md]` `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/authentication/site-token.md]` `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/authentication/workspace-token.md]` `[SOURCE: https://github.com/webflow/mcp-server]`\n- Scopes are resource-specific and should be minimized; OAuth install scopes must be registered, workspace tokens do not provide site scope, and site tokens cannot access custom-code endpoints. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/scopes.md]`\n- Official guidance supports secure storage, minimal scopes, rotation, and revocation. Webflow documents a Beta MCP server but no isolated staging sandbox or non-production credential class in the sources consulted. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/v2.0.0/reference/oauth-app.md]` `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/mcp/reference/getting-started.md]`\n\n## Iteration 4: Operational constraints and changelog evolution\n\n- Data API limits are plan-based: 60 requests/minute for Starter/Basic, 120 for CMS/eCommerce/Business, and custom for Enterprise. Responses expose `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, `X-RateLimit-Limit`, and `Retry-After`; endpoint-specific limits can be stricter. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/rate-limits]`\n- CMS collection-item listing uses offset pagination with a maximum `limit` of 100 and a `pagination` object containing `total`, `limit`, and `offset`; this is endpoint-scoped evidence, not a universal claim. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/docs/working-with-the-cms/manage-collections-and-items.md]`\n- Errors use standard HTTP classes and a structured `code`/`message`/`externalReference`/`details` response. SDKs provide exponential backoff and custom clients should honor `Retry-After`; no idempotency-key or replay guarantee was documented in the consulted official references. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/error-handling.md]` `[INFERENCE: absence of idempotency-key and replay semantics in consulted official references]`\n- Publishing requires `sites:write`, explicit domain or Webflow-subdomain inputs, and is limited to one successful publish queue per minute; staging-to-production publishing can include all staged changes. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/data/reference/sites/publish]`\n- Webflow changed the `translatable` parameter from boolean semantics on July 27 to a target secondary-locale ID on July 29, making booleans return 400 and adding documented 403/500 cases. `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/27.md]` `[SOURCE: https://developers.webflow.com/home/changelog/2026/7/29.md]`","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":17,"totalLines":17,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/015-mcp-webflow/001-deep-research/research/lineages/luna-fast/research.md","time":{"start":1785694043529,"end":1785694043536}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0b231802796e93c5016a6f875a92748191a6e9effbb14f4e50"}},"id":"prt_fc3a8bd2c001CT9GGqBVMB4Gtp","sessionID":"ses_03c78660bffecT9HS5m59QDUL4","messageID":"msg_fc3a89840001uI09CAituZq07G"}}
